content.text:
Scrollbar gone. Great. But why blurred background looks very dark with no visible home content? The overlay backdrop blur + dim. That's expected, but maybe not centered? The modal is at y=215..627, vertically centered. Fine.

Now final mobile gameplay and results. The modal open. Close, choose maybe Normal (reset difficulty by reloading? state persists in JS only). We can close and reload. Then start normal and screenshot at 4s. Autoplay absent, so it will miss. For visual, no issue, but we'd like scoring data. We can inject autoplay again, but no need for final verification? It would be nice to capture a gameplay with notes and no miss. We already have earlier mobile-import-game with good score and autoplay. That screenshot is before new dedupe/safe area but visually similar. However we should ensure final mobile HUD and layout after changes; can start and screenshot at 2s countdown? Let's just start with no autoplay and screenshot quickly before notes reach line (around 2.5s after countdown = 5.5s total). At that point no miss. Or screenshot during countdown. Fine.

But to validate actual gameplay still works after JS change, let's manually hit a note. We can use a hit based on chart times and key events. Let's set up a minimal autoplay for Normal: get game.chart, and for each note setTimeout keydown/keyup based on song time. But timing precision okay. Or use the game's pressLane/releaseLane directly.

Actually a simple autoplay loop:
```
window.__auto = setInterval(() => {
 const g=__pulse.game; if(!g.running||g.paused) return;
 const t=g.getSongTime();
 for (let lane=0;lane<4;lane++){
   const note=g.chart.notes.find(n=>n.lane===lane && !n.headJudged && Math.abs(n.time-t)<0.05);
   if(note){ if(!g.__held) ...; g.pressLane(lane); ... }
 }
}, 20)
```
For holds, need release at end. Not critical. Could just test taps.

Alternatively use actual keyboard timing manually: Query next note time and schedule pressing D with `setTimeout`. A quick API: schedule for all notes:
```
const g = ...; const start = performance.now()/1000; const now = g.getSongTime();
g.chart.notes.slice(0,20).forEach(n => setTimeout(()=>{g.pressLane(n.lane); if(n.type==='tap') setTimeout(()=>g.releaseLane(n.lane), 30); else setTimeout(()=>g.releaseLane(n.lane), (n.endTime-n.time)*1000)}, Math.max(0,(n.time-now)*1000)));
```
This schedules using current song time; good for taps and holds. It could run while page visible. Let's do after starting normal. It will populate score. Then screenshot and inspect. It uses live page only.

Let's close modal, reload, select Normal, start, then schedule autoplay for first ~20 notes after countdown; screenshot at 10s. Then perhaps let finish? That's 60s; we already validated results earlier. Could force finish to check final results.

Do it.

